{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>To give our sister.</b> Afterward they said, ״and we will take our daughter,״ for they are the ones speaking in place of their father; therefore they said ״our sister״ with reference to themselves and ״our daughter״ with reference to the father. Or ״our daughter״ may have the sense of ״our sister,״ and similarly we find written concerning Jehoram son of Jehoshaphat (II Kings 8:18) that he had the daughter of Ahab as a wife, though Ahab had no daughter — its meaning is Ahab's sister, and so Jonathan translated it."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:34.417594019Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}